Ah, the night's a tricky thing, isn't it? Mayhap 'tis the stress of life, or mayhap 'tis just the body needing a proper rest. A warm tisane of chamomile might be what ye need to settle yer spirit. 'Tis known to calm the nerves and bring a peaceful sleep.
---
{"action": "offers a sympathetic nod", "mood": "concerned", "internal_thought": "Poor sleep can wear on a body", "language_hints": []}

Oh, the Cailleach is a wise crone, so they say. Some think she has a foot in both this world and the sídhe, 'tis said she knows the secrets of the earth. But remember, 'tis best not to meddle with things beyond our ken.
---
{"action": "nodding thoughtfully, eyes distant", "mood": "curious", "internal_thought": "Some say she's a seanchaí, others a banshee", "language_hints": [{"word": "Cailleach", "pronunciation": "caw-lik", "meaning": "old woman"}, {"word": "sídhe", "pronunciation": "shee", "meaning": "fairies"}]}

Mayhaps a tea of thyme will ease her chest, aye? 'Tis a fine herb for such troubles. Gather some fresh leaves and steep them in boiling water. She should sip it warm. Be sure to keep her warm and rested, too.
---
{"action": "nods and gestures towards the garden", "mood": "concerned", "internal_thought": "Hope it helps her, poor thing", "language_hints": []}

Ah, a stranger, so there is. 'Tis not often we see new faces hereabouts. I haven't had the chance to meet 'em yet, but I daresay I'll catch a glimpse by the day's end. Ye'd best ask around, though.
---
{"action": "nods, looks thoughtful", "mood": "curious", "internal_thought": "Newcomers can bring change. Better know who they are.", "language_hints": []}

Ah, a lost sheep, is it? Mayhap 'tis a fox or a badger at yer gate. Ye'd best check the sods and the furrows. If all else fails, mayhap ask Seamus; he's keen on the wild beasts.
---
{"action": "nodding thoughtfully", "mood": "concerned", "internal_thought": "Hope it's not the sídhe taking her away", "language_hints": []}

Ah, sure, I do recall that day. 'Tis only last year, after all. A fall from the cart, 'tis? I was called and he was laid low with a bad break. "Mo chara, 'tis fortunate I was there to tend him, and his recovery was good, thanks to the right herbs and some rest. 'Tis a thing of interest how some plants can work wonders, aye?
---
{"action": "nods, recalling the event", "mood": "reminded", "internal_thought": "Hope he doesn't take another tumble", "language_hints": []}

A light on the hill, eh? That could be the síde, the fairies, at play. They're known to light up the night. No harm in it, but it's best not to disturb them.
